dogwater32 - A CPU emulator with a typed asm

Instruction Word Layout


+----------------+---------------+---------------+-----------------------+
|     OPCODE     |      RD       |      RS       |       UNUSED          |
+----------------+---------------+---------------+-----------------------+
   6 bits          4 bits          4 bits        18 bits

Instruction Set

CONTROL
-------
NOP         - No operation
HLT         - Halt execution
INT         - Software interrupt
DIS_INT     - Disable interrupts
ENA_INT     - Enable interrupts

ARITHMETIC
----------
ADD / ADDI  - Add register or immediate
SUB / SUBI  - Subtract register or immediate
INC / DEC   - Increment / decrement
MUL / MULI  - Multiply register or immediate
DIV / DIVI  - Divide register or immediate
MOD / MODI  - Modulo register or immediate

BITWISE / LOGIC
---------------
AND / ANDI   - Bitwise AND
NAND / NANDI - Bitwise NAND
NOR / NORI   - Bitwise NOR
OR / ORI     - Bitwise OR
XOR / XORI   - Bitwise XOR
NOT          - Bitwise NOT

COMPARISON
----------
CMP          - Compare registers
CMPI         - Compare register with immediate

SHIFT / ROTATE
--------------
SHL / SHLI   - Shift left (logical)
SHR / SHRI   - Shift right (logical)
SAR / SARI   - Shift right (arithmetic)

CONTROL FLOW
------------
JMP          - Jump to address
JZ           - Jump if zero flag set
JNZ          - Jump if zero flag not set
JN           - Jump if negative flag set
CALL         - Call subroutine
RET          - Return from subroutine

DATA MOVEMENT
-------------
MOV          - Move register to register
MOVK         - Move register to keyboard register
RMOVK        - Move keyboard register to register
LI           - Load immediate into register
READ         - Read from memory
WRITE        - Write to memory
PUSH         - Push register to stack
POP          - Pop from stack to register
SWAP_R       - Swap registers
SWAP_M       - Swap with memory

VARIABLES AND DEFINES
---------------------
#define DEFINE_NAME #0xVAL
VAR_NAME: dd VAR_VAL

REGISTERS
---------
 0  : R0   (GP)
 1  : R1   (GP)
 2  : R2   (Reserved - used by interrupts)
 3  : R3   (GP)
 4  : R4   (GP)
 5  : R5   (GP)
 6  : R6   (GP)
 7  : R7   (LR - pointer for CALL/RET)
 8  : R8   (GP)
 9  : R9   (GP)
10  : R10  (GP)
11  : R11  (GP)
12  : R12  (GP)
13  : R13  (GP)
14  : R14  (GP)
15  : R15  (GP)

SPECIAL REGISTER
----------------
 keyboard_reg : Holds input/output state for keyboard device

INTERRUPTS
----------

There are currently 5 Interrupts which are:

KEYBOARD_READ (INT 0x0): reads a char to keyboard_reg
KEYBOARD_WRITE (INT 0x1): prints a char from keyboard_reg
NMI (INT 0x2): this will stop the cpu without any error message
MEMORY_FAULT (INT 0x3): used by memory function, this should not be used by programs
WAIT_MS (INT 0x4) : this will wait till R2 ms
